<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Handan</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Handan is a city in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hebei">Hebei</a>, at the foot of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taihang-mountains">Taihang Mountains</a>. It was the capital of the State of Zhao from 386 BCE until its capture by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qin-dynasty">Qin</a> in 228 BCE, and a great commercial city of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/warring-states-period">Warring States period</a>. Its resistance to the Qin siege of 259–257 BCE, relieved by armies of Wei and Chu, is one of the famous episodes of the era.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/handan.jpg" alt="Handan" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: H2v5o68z · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E6%AD%A6%E7%81%B5%E4%B8%9B%E5%8F%B0_10.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
